<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27821" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δογμᾰτ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>for doctrines, didactic,</i> [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διάλογοι</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Quint.
				<u>Inst.</u>
				2.15.26
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of persons,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ἰατροί</span> physicians <i>who
				go by general principles,</i> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμπειρικοί</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεθοδικοί,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				<u>Ther.Praef.</u>
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				1.65
			</span></i>; in Philosophy, <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>M.</u>
				7.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				9.70
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ὑπολήψεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					9.83
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. φιλοσοφία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.E.
					<u>P.</u>
					1.4
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.L.
					9.74
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>P.</u>
				1.197
			</span></i>: 
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κώτερον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>M.</u>
					6.4
				</span></i>
			.</div>
